# L §5.11 step 1: "Givens. If a given of x (a version row given x[…] = …) matches k by the read rule (§4.6), return
# it. A with or as if pin wins over a given."  L §8.2: "given: <def>[keys] = v (<version>) ... printed once as
# written, with its key range if it has one".  The rule would give 0; the given at a gives 1; the pin wins: 5.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = [a, b]
input five: int

def q[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = 0

version g
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  given q[a] = 1
  five = 5

ask q1: q[a], q[b] law 2026-06-30
ask q2: q[a] with q[a] = five law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (1, 0)
  given: q[a] = 1 (g)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2: 5
  pinned: q[a] = 5
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
